# Blender 5.2.0 LTS MTL File: 'cokecan.blend'
# www.blender.org
#
# HAND-EDITED AFTER EXPORT -- RE-APPLY AFTER ANY RE-EXPORT FROM BLENDER, which
# overwrites this file.
#
# The can renders crisp in Blender and in Windows 3D Viewer and washed out in
# RViz, and the material is why. Blender's OBJ exporter writes a large Ka
# (0.48 on the label, 1.0 on the metal), which means nothing in the PBR
# pipeline the model came from -- PBR has no ambient term, so those viewers
# ignore it. Ogre, which is what RViz draws with, honours it literally and adds
# Ka * ambient_light flat to every pixel. Roughly a quarter of full white laid
# over the label, which lifts the reds toward grey: exactly "washed out".
#
# Ks 0.5 at Ns 656 is the same story from the other end -- a very tight, very
# bright highlight, which on a cylinder is a hard white stripe down the side.
#
# illum 3 asks for a ray-traced reflection model. Nothing in this scene
# reflects, so 2 (specular, no reflection) is what is actually wanted.
#
# Kd was absent from the label material entirely. With a diffuse texture bound
# that usually works out, but it leaves the modulating colour up to whatever
# the loader defaults to. Stating it as white makes the texture pass through
# unchanged rather than by luck.
#
# Changed from the export: Ns, Ka, Ks, illum, and an added Kd. Nothing else,
# and no geometry or UVs are affected.

newmtl Insert_Label_Here
Ns 60.000000
Ka 0.100000 0.100000 0.100000
Kd 1.000000 1.000000 1.000000
Ks 0.120000 0.120000 0.120000
Ke 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
Ni 1.450000
d 1.000000
illum 2
map_Kd cocacolacanimage.jpg

newmtl Metal_part
Ns 60.000000
Ka 0.100000 0.100000 0.100000
Kd 0.369412 0.369412 0.369412
Ks 0.200000 0.200000 0.200000
Ke 0.000000 0.000000 0.000000
Ni 1.450000
d 1.000000
illum 2
